1. **Convert pounds to kilograms**:
   \[
   \text{kilograms} = \frac{\text{pounds}}{2.205} = \frac{32 \text{ lbs}}{2.205} \approx 14.40 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. **Calculate the total loading dose**:
   \[
   \text{Loading dose} = \text{Loading dose per kg} \times \text{Body weight in kg} = 20 \text{ mg/kg} \times 14.40 \text{ kg} = 288 \text{ mg}
   \]

3. **Calculate the time required for the infusion**:
   \[
   \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Total loading data}}{\text{Flow rate}} = \frac{288 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 576 \text{ min}
   \]

The total time required to administer the loading dose is \(\boxed{576 \text{ minutes}}\).
