ΔFe = 340 kJ/mol
ΔCl = 381 kJ/mol

The reaction can be represented as:

Fe(H20)62+ + 2Cl1 → [FeCl4]2+ + 2H20

The standard enthalpy change (ΔH) for this reaction can be calculated using the following formula:

ΔH = Σ(ΔH_obs_i) - Σ(ΔH_obs_i)

