- Initial concentration of iron (III) chloride (Fe) = 1.0 M
- Initial concentration of KCN = 0.25 moles (we need to convert this to concentration)
- K$_{eq}$ = 1.2 x 10$^{20}$

First, we need to calculate the concentration of KNC added to the reaction. Assuming the volume of the solution is 1 mole (since the initial concentration of Fe is 1.0 M), the concentration of KNC added is 0.25 moles / 1 mole = 1.0 M.

