   \]
4. **Counting Principle (Additivity) for Infinite Countable Events:** For a countable collection of disjoint events $\{A_i\}$, the probability of their union is the sum of their individual probabilities:
   \[
   \mathbb{P}\left(\bigcup_{i=1}^{\infty} A_i\right) = \sum_{i=1}^{\infty} \mathbb{P}(A_i) \quad \text{if } A_i \cap A_j = \emptyset \quad \text{for all } i \neq j.
