","The negation of the proposition ""If $A \cup B = A$, then $A \cap B = B$"" is:

$$ \neg (A \cup B = A \rightarrow A \cap B = B) $$

The negation of a biconditional statement $p \rightarrow q$ is $p \land \neg q$. Applying this to our negation, we get:

$$ (A \cup B = A) \land \neg (A \cap B = B) $$

This can be simplified to:

$$ (A \cup B = A) \land (A \cap B \neq B) $$

Thus, the answer is: $\boxed{A \cup B = A \land A \cap B \neq B}$.",fluency,"# Task Description
