\[
Q^2 = (P_f - P_i)^2 = (E_f/c, \mathbf{p}_f) - (E_i/c, \mathbf{p}_i)^2
\]
Expanding the square of a four-momentum:
\[
(P_f - P_i)^2 = (E_f/c - E_i/c)^2 - (P_f - P_i) \cdot (P_f - P_i)
\]
Expanding the dot product:
\[
(P_f - P_i) \cdot (P_f - P_i) = (E_f/c - E_i/c)^2 - (P_f \cdot P_f - P_f \ \mathbf{p}_i + P_i \ \mathbf{p}_f - P_i \ \mathbf{p}_i)
\]
Using the definition \( P_i \cdot P_i = E_i^2 - P_i^2 \) and \( P_f \cdot P_f = E_f^2 - P_f^2 \):
\[
(P_f - P_i) \cdot (P_f - P_i) = E_f^2 - P_f^2 - E_i^2 + P_i^2 - P_f \ \mathbf{p}_i + P_i \ \mathbf{p}_f
\]
Substituting back into the expression for \( Q^2 \):
\[
Q^2 = (E_f/c - E_i/c)^2 - (E_f^2 - P_f^2 - E_i^2 + P_i^2 - P_f \ \mathbf{p}_i + P_i \ \mathbf{p}_f)
\]
Simplifying the terms:
\[
Q^2 = \left(\frac{E_f - E_i}{c}\right)^2 - (E_f^2 - P_f^2 - E_i^2 + P_i^2 - P_f \ \mathbf{p}_i + P_i \ \mathbf{p}_f)
