   \[
   A = \begin{bmatrix} \epsilon_x & \gamma_{xy}/2 \\ \gamma_{xy}/2 & \epsilon_y \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} -0.0005 & 0.0015 \\ 0.0015 & 0.0035 \end{bmatrix}
   \]
   The eigenvalues are found by solving the characteristic equation: \( \det(A - \lambda I) = 0 \), where \( \lambda \) are the eigenvalues and \( I \) is the identity matrix.
   \[
   \begin{vmatrix} -0.0005 - \lambda & 0.0015 \\ 0.0015 & 0.0035 - \lambda \end{vmatrix} = 0
   \]
