For a loop with \( n \) turns, the formula becomes:

\[
B = \frac{2\pi I n}{r}
\]

Substituting the given values:
- \( I = 1 \, \text{A} \)
- \( r = 0.2 \, \text{m} \)
- \( n = 100 \, \text{turns} \)

\[
B = \frac{2\pi \times 1 \, \text{A} \times 100}{0.2 \, \text{m}} = \frac{200\pi}{0.2} \, \text{N/m} = 1000\pi \, \text{N/m}
\]

Approximating \( \pi \approx 3.14159 \):

\[
B \approx 1000 \times 3.14159 \, \text{N/m} \approx 3141.59 \, \text{N/m}
\]

