(a) What is the magnitude of the acceleration of the proton?  
(b) How long does it take the proton to reach a speed of \(35,000 \, \text{m/s}\)?
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
(a) The force \( F \) exerted by the electric field on the proton is given by:  
\[
F = k_0 \cdot q \cdot E,
\]  
where \( k_0 = 1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C} \) is the magnitude of the charge of the proton, \( E = 500 \, \text{N/C} \) is the electric field strength, and \( g = 1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C} \) is the magnitude of the charge of the proton.  

Substituting the values:  
\[
F = 1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C} \times 500 \, \text{N/C} = 800 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{N} = 8 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}.
\]  

The acceleration \( a \) of the projectile is then found using Newton's second law:  
\[
a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{8 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} \approx 4.8 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2.
\]  

(b) The velocity \( v \) of the projectile after a time \( t \) is given by:  
\[
v = v_0 + at,
\]  
where \( v_0 = 0 \, \text{m/s} \) is the initial velocity.  

