\[
t = \frac{v - v_0}{a} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s} - 0 \, \text{m/s}}{4.8 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2} \approx 0.725 \, \text{s}.
\]  

**Final Answers**:  
(a) The magnitude of the acceleration of the proton is \(\boxed{4.8 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2}\).  
(b) It takes the proton approximately \(\boxed{0.725 \, \text{s}}\) to reach a speed of \(35,000 \, \text{m/s}\).
