Given that the clock in the cockpit shows a time of 3 years when the ship returns to Earth, we can use this time as \( t_s \). Therefore, the time observed on the Earth's clock is:
\[
t_e = \sqrt{2} \times 3 \text{ years} \approx 4.29 \text{ years}
\]
