m is the mass of the object (in this case, the mass of the pulley)
a_t is the tangential acceleration of the point P on the rim of the pulley

Given:
Mass of the pulley (m) = 1 kg
Radius of the pulley (r) = 0.5 m
Tangangular acceleration (a_t) = 2 m/s^2

Now, we can plug the values into the formula:

